<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-to-build`>>

!! What to build
A. Broker (ceremony-broker.js), the unanswered claim ends on an EVENT, never a timer (no setTimeout/setInterval anywhere):
* `vessel:withdraw{tabSession}` from the claimant's own client (source.id === claim.clientId and claim.tabSession matches) deletes that claim and calls its release. From any other client it ends nothing.
* At the top of EVERY message event (any route, before routing), sweep: `self.clients.matchAll({type:"window"})`, and for each held vessel claim whose clientId no longer appears, delete it and release it. Hold the sweep under that event's waitUntil. A live claim stays.
* Keep the header comment true (one line naming both ends).
B. Protocol (vessel-protocol.ts): PageToVessel gains `{ t: "port:want"; wantId: string; tabSession: string }`; VesselToPage gains `{ t: "port:minted"; wantId: string; port?: MessagePort; refused?: string }`.
C. Host (vessel-host.ts, inside `connect`'s receive switch): `case "port:want"`:
* if this connection holds no session (no hello / conn.session null) post `{ t: "port:minted", wantId, refused: "session-unadmitted" }` and stop.
* else mint `new MessageChannel()`; call `this host's own connect` (the same `connect` function of the returned object — hoist it to a named const so the case can call it) with a scope `{ postMessage: (m, t=[]) => port1.postMessage(m, t) }`; wire `port1.onmessage = (e) => c.receive(e.data)`; `port1.start()` is implied by onmessage. Post `{ t: "port:minted", wantId, port: port2 }` with transfer `[port2]` to the owner's page.
* The minted connection opens NO session until its own `hello` arrives over port1 (connect already does that); its asks go to port1 (its own door), never the owner's scope.
* A `ceremony:port` arriving over port1 carries `port` in e.data (transferred); connect's existing `ceremony:port` case handles it.
* When the owner's connection closes, minted ports it handed stay their own connections (no coupling needed in this step).

<<~/ahu>>

